#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""pr-audit: an independent re-check of the READY verdict on acmeapp_nextjs pull requests.

  pr-audit weekly [--count 10] [--include 4771,...] [--exclude 4777,...] [--prs a,b,c]
  pr-audit daily  [--max 8] [--dry-run]
  pr-audit sources <run-dir> [--mode weekly|daily]  source changes from a finished run, no new audits
  pr-audit report <run-dir> [--mode weekly|daily]   re-render a report from a finished run
  pr-audit selftest                                 sealing and parsing checks, no network
  pr-audit db <table> '<query>' [...]               read-only rows, the audit sessions' only DB door

Each pull request gets two fresh `claude -p` sessions:

  blind    sees the sanitized description, the diff, the source at the audited commit, CI and the
           attached evidence. It has no GitHub credentials. It writes its own gaps and verdict.
  compare  runs after the blind verdict is on disk and hashed. Only then does this script fetch the
           READY comment, the sealed body sections and the post-merge history.

Then the source step turns the finished audits into ranked changes to the prompts and scripts behind
READY, and each change is replayed against each pull request's record. That list opens the report.

This script only reads GitHub: gh() refuses anything but read commands. Docs: docs/pr-audit.md.
"""
